        new("embedded-views",
            "Where are Spec Explorer, Task Explorer, Flow View, Traceability View, and Architecture View?",
            "<p><strong>Spec Explorer</strong> tabs (Flow View, Traceability View, Architecture View, Spec Explorer) are embedded inside <strong>Specification Review</strong> (<a href='/extract'>/extract</a>) and appear automatically after a successful spec analysis.</p><p><strong>Task Explorer</strong> exists in two forms:</p><ul><li><strong>Standalone Task Explorer</strong> (<a href='/task-explorer'>/task-explorer</a>) — a dedicated menu item in the Analysis section. Upload or paste a tasks.md file to explore the implementation plan independently of any spec alignment.</li><li><strong>Task Explorer tab inside Implementation Review</strong> (<a href='/task-alignment'>/task-alignment</a>) — the same explorer enriched with spec alignment data after a full analysis. Use this when you want to explore tasks in the context of their spec coverage and risk.</li></ul><p>Once analysis is complete, switching tabs does not require re-uploading files — the session is preserved automatically. See the <a href='#discovery'>Feature Discovery</a> section for full details.</p>"),

        new("drift-vs-review",
            "What is the difference between Spec Drift and Implementation Review?",
