            "<p>Use <strong>Task Deltas</strong> when your implementation plan changes between sprints or planning iterations — for example when new tasks are added, existing tasks are expanded in scope, or tasks are removed.</p><p>It helps you answer: <em>What changed in our implementation plan, and what is the risk?</em> It is especially useful when AI generates or rewrites a tasks.md and you want to understand what shifted.</p>"),

        new("spec-linked",
            "What does Spec Linked mean?",
            "<p><strong>Spec Linked</strong> (shown in Implementation Review's Spec Alignment tab) means the analysis found a strong connection between the task and one or more items in the specification — through direct spec ID references (FR-001, US-03), matching CamelCase entity names, or significant keyword overlap.</p><p>A score of 6 or higher is required for Linked status. It does not guarantee complete coverage — it means the task appears to be working on documented requirements.</p>"),

        new("needs-review",
            "What does Needs Review mean?",
