        new("regression-candidate",
            "What is a Regression Candidate?",
            "<p>A <strong>Regression Candidate</strong> is a task flagged as likely to require regression testing before release. A task becomes a Regression Candidate if it:</p><ul><li>Has <strong>High Risk</strong> classification, or</li><li>Touches a high-sensitivity area: <strong>Security, Authorization, Audit, or Domain Events</strong>, or</li><li>Has <strong>Medium Risk</strong> and the analysis has recommended tests for it.</li></ul><p>The Regression Candidates KPI card and filter chip in the Risk &amp; Testing tab give you a focused list to include in your regression suite.</p>"),

        new("technical-only",
            "Why are Technical Only tasks valid?",
            "<p>Not every development task needs a specification item. <strong>Technical Only</strong> tasks are infrastructure, scaffolding, configuration, refactoring, or tooling tasks that do not introduce externally visible behaviour.</p><p>Examples: adding a NuGet package, setting up CI/CD, configuring appsettings.json. These are valid tasks — they just do not need spec coverage. Low Risk Technical Only tasks require no action.</p><p>Important configuration tasks (auth URLs, service bus connections, external APIs) are still classified as Technical Only but get <strong>Medium Risk</strong> — because incorrect configuration can affect runtime behaviour.</p>"),

